  "assessment": [
    "All final-source samples and expected refusals passed. Current full-scenario medians were 40.453-42.546 ms; the MSRV compatibility run median was 39.242 ms.",
    "Current initial transition/commit/publication medians were 0.729-0.751 ms; the dispatch-return-to-durable-completion leg was 4.088-4.180 ms; verified result/causation to machine commit/publication was 1.632-1.743 ms. All tails and outliers remain in raw observations.",
    "The measured scenario deliberately includes fresh databases, recovery, fsync, console output and cleanup. Timed callbacks add clock/observer work. No timer subtraction, outlier removal, statistical equivalence or baseline regression conclusion.",
    "Native execution cost includes IPC, host polling, durable writes and fencing. Worker CPU/business computation is not independently timed. Saga external effects are not executed.",
    "This is an unsaturated sequential composition profile. It does not measure queue-full refusal latency, runtime saturation, concurrent independent-machine throughput, isolated effect CPU cost or a sustained service-level capacity guarantee. Existing bound/refusal correctness tests remain separate; backpressure performance coverage remains open.",
    "Whole-process/child GNU time maximum RSS is retained in KiB; it is not simultaneous summed host+worker memory. Allocations and stack usage are not measured.",
    "CPU pinning does not isolate frequency or other system load; chaos is running on CPUs8-15. OS caches and other load remain uncontrolled. This is selected profile evidence, not exact release qualification."
  ],
